  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "HTML Table Headers"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Table headers are defined with th elements.\nEach th element represents a table cell."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Firstname</th>\n\n  <th>Lastname</th>\n    <th>Age</th>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Jill</td>\n    <td>Smith</td>\n\n  <td>50</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Eve</td>\n\n  <td>Jackson</td>\n    <td>94</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table_th"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Vertical Table Headers"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To use the first column as table headers, define the first cell in each row as a\n<th> element:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Firstname</th>\n\n  <td>Jill</td>\n    <td>Eve</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n  <th>Lastname</th>\n    <td>Smith</td>\n\n  <td>Jackson</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Age</th>\n    <td>94</td>\n\n  <td>50</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table_th_vertical"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Align Table Headers"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "By default, table headers are bold and centered:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Firstname",
    "Lastname",
    "Age"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Jill",
     "Smith",
     "50"
    ],
    [
     "Eve",
     "Jackson",
     "94"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To left-align the table headers, use the CSS text-align property:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": "th {\n  text-align: left;\n\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table_th_align"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Header for Multiple Columns"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can have a header that spans over two or more columns."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Name",
    "Age"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "Jill",
     "Smith",
     "50"
    ],
    [
     "Eve",
     "Jackson",
     "94"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To do this, use the colspan attribute on the\n<th> element:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th colspan=\"2\">Name</th>\n    <th>Age</th>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Jill</td>\n    <td>Smith</td>\n\n  <td>50</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Eve</td>\n\n  <td>Jackson</td>\n    <td>94</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_table_th_colspan"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "You will learn more about colspan and rowspan in the Table colspan & rowspan chapter."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Table Caption"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "You can add a caption that serves as a heading for the entire table."
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Month",
    "Savings"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "January",
     "$100"
    ],
    [
     "February",
     "$50"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To add a caption to a table, use the <caption> tag:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<table style=\"width:100%\">\n  <caption>Monthly savings</caption>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Month</th>\n    <th>Savings</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>January</td>\n    <td>$100</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>February</td>\n    <td>$50</td>\n  </tr>\n\n </table>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_tables2"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "The <caption> tag\nshould be inserted immediately after the <table> tag."
  }
 ]
}